# ai.readme — Briefing for AI Agents Working on This Repo

**Audience:** an AI coding assistant (Claude, GPT, Copilot, etc.) picking up this repo cold
and being asked to make changes. This file exists so you can get oriented without a human
walkthrough.

**If you are a human, read `README.md` instead.** This file is denser, more opinionated, and
assumes you can follow code across files without hand-holding.

---

## 1. Project in one paragraph

This is the marketing / recruitment / legacy site for **Washington University in St. Louis
Design-Build-Fly** (DBF), a student aircraft competition team. It is a **Next.js 14 App
Router** project configured for **static export** (`output: 'export'` in `next.config.js`).
The site is content-driven: almost all copy, image paths, roster data, and per-team config
live as plain JS object literals under `data/`. Components under `components/` read those
objects and render them. There is **no backend, no DB, no runtime server** — `npm run build`
emits plain HTML/CSS/JS into `out/`, which is uploaded to **DreamHost** via SFTP/rsync.

Repo: `https://github.com/cifyr/DBFApp`. Main branch: `main`.

---

## 2. Environment constraints (read before coding)

| Constraint | Detail |
| --- | --- |
| **Node version** | Use **Node 20 or 22**. Node 24 is broken — Next 14.2's `require-hook.js` throws `ERR_INVALID_PACKAGE_CONFIG` intermittently against the bundled `dist/compiled/*/package.json` files. On macOS: `brew install node@22` and put `/opt/homebrew/opt/node@22/bin` first in PATH. |
| **Next version** | 14.2.x (currently resolves to 14.2.35). Do not upgrade to 15.x casually — would touch the App Router conventions and force changes across every route. |
| **Package manager** | npm (there is a `package-lock.json`). Don't introduce yarn/pnpm without a reason. |
| **iCloud Desktop sync** | The working copy lives under `~/Desktop`, which is iCloud-synced. iCloud occasionally desyncs files inside `node_modules/` and `vendor/framer-motion/`, producing "Module not found" errors mid-build. If you see module-resolution errors that look impossible, reinstall deps or re-extract the vendored tarball (see §6). |
| **Static export** | No API routes, no server actions, no `fetch` with caching at request time, no `cookies()`/`headers()` reads. If the task requires any of those, you have to redesign it (e.g. external API) or push back on the requirement. |

---

## 3. File-by-file map

```
app/
├── layout.js                     Root <html>/<body>, metadata, mounts AppShell
├── layout 2.js                   STALE iCloud duplicate — ignore, don't edit
├── globals.css                   CSS variables (--color-*, --space-*, --text-*, --font-*, --shadow-*, --radius-*)
├── page.js                       Homepage — composes Hero, MissionSection, WhoWeAre,
│                                 PolaroidGallery (past aircraft), MeetThePresidents,
│                                 MeetTheTeams, JoinSection, Sponsors, SocialCTA, Footer
├── join/page.js                  /join
├── partners/page.js              /partners
├── photos/page.js                /photos — internal dashboard
└── team/[slug]/page.js           /team/:slug — dynamic, uses generateStaticParams()
                                  Renders AdminContent for slug='admin', else SubTeamContent

components/
├── AppShell.js                   Client wrapper: sets up Lenis smooth scroll + GSAP
│                                 ScrollTrigger, handles hash scroll, page-transition context
├── Navbar.js / Footer.js         Site chrome; data from data/homeContent.js
├── Hero.js                       Homepage hero (GSAP animations)
├── MissionSection.js             Homepage mission block
├── WhoWeAre.js                   Homepage "who we are" block
├── PolaroidGallery.js            Homepage past-aircraft polaroid gallery + modal
├── MeetThePresidents.js          Homepage presidents row
├── MeetTheTeams.js               Homepage team grid with per-team cards
├── JoinSection.js                Homepage join CTA
├── Sponsors.js                   Homepage sponsor logos
├── SocialCTA.js                  Homepage social CTA block (uses next/image)
├── ProgressiveHeadshot.js        <img> with blur-in load + initial-based fallback
├── PageTransition.js             Context + overlay for route transitions
├── TransitionLink.js             <Link> wrapper that triggers the transition overlay
└── templates/
    ├── SubTeamHero.js            Team-page hero
    ├── SubTeamContent.js         Regular team layout: about + carousel + leaders + TeamLegacy
    ├── AdminContent.js           Special layout for /team/admin
    ├── TeamCarousel.js           Per-team image carousel.
    │                             Auto-detects portrait vs landscape from each slide's
    │                             natural dimensions and switches caption position:
    │                               portrait  → caption on the right, 50/50 split
    │                               landscape → caption below, min-height = max carousel height
    │                             Mobile (≤768px) collapses portrait layout to stacked.
    ├── TeamLegacy.js             Legacy & leadership grid (per-team)
    └── Templates.module.css      Styles for the entire templates/ family

data/                             ⭐ Content layer. Modify here for 90% of requests.
├── homeContent.js                Home page copy, nav, footer, brand, past aircraft,
│                                 sponsors, join text. Exports `homeContent` (large object).
├── teamData.js                   Array of team configs (slug, title, description,
│                                 heroImage, about, carousel, ...).
│                                 Also exports teamCarouselMedia keyed by slug.
├── people.js                     Exports:
│                                 - presidents (array)
│                                 - teamLeaders (object keyed by team slug)
│                                 - adminLeaders (array)
│                                 - formatPersonAcademicInfo(person) helper
└── photos.js                     Exports `photos` — nested object of asset paths.
                                  Source of truth for all image URLs.

lib/
└── framer-motion.js              Re-export shim: `export * from '../vendor/framer-motion/dist/es/index.mjs'`.
                                  **Always import framer-motion APIs from '@/lib/framer-motion',
                                  never from 'framer-motion' directly** — the direct package can
                                  become partially desynced by iCloud.

vendor/
└── framer-motion/                Unpacked copy of framer-motion@11.18.2. Source is
                                  framer-motion-11.18.2.tgz at repo root; re-extract if broken.

scripts/
├── prepare-next-runtime.mjs      Symlinks ./.next (or ./.next-dev) to /tmp/dbfapp-next-runtime/
│                                 Runs automatically via predev/prebuild hooks.
└── clean-runtime-state.mjs       Removes those symlinks.

public/
├── images/                       General site images (2018.jpg, 2019.jpeg, home.jpg, etc.)
├── images/Carousel/              Carousel images referenced by data/teamData.js
├── headshots/                    People photos referenced by data/people.js via data/photos.js
├── frames/                       UI frame assets
└── plane.svg                     Homepage plane graphic

next.config.js                    output: 'export', trailingSlash: true, images.unoptimized: true
jsconfig.json                     "@/*" → "./*" path alias
package.json                      Scripts: dev, build, start, predev, prebuild, clean:runtime
framer-motion-11.18.2.tgz         Source for vendor/framer-motion — do not delete
out/                              Build output, gitignored
```

---

## 4. Conventions & contracts

### Imports
- Always import modules via the `@/` alias for paths relative to repo root.
- **Framer Motion must come from `@/lib/framer-motion`**, never the npm package directly.
- CSS Modules: `import styles from './Thing.module.css'`. Don't rename classes without
  updating the `.module.css` pair.

### Styling
- Tokens in `app/globals.css`. Examples: `var(--color-navy)`, `var(--space-lg)`,
  `var(--text-xl)`, `var(--shadow-md)`, `var(--radius-lg)`, `var(--color-caption)`.
- Prefer existing tokens over hardcoded values. If you must hardcode, stay consistent with
  nearby code.
- No Tailwind, no styled-components, no emotion. Don't introduce a new styling system.
- Responsive breakpoint currently in use: `@media (max-width: 768px)`.

### Data shape expectations

- `data/homeContent.js` is a single giant object with many subtrees. Preserve its shape when
  editing — components dereference specific keys (`homeContent.pastAircraft.aircraft`,
  `homeContent.teamsSection.teams`, etc.). Rename a key → something breaks silently.
- `data/teamData.js` exports `teamData` (array). Each item:
  ```ts
  {
    slug: string,            // URL segment; also used as key in teamLeaders
    title: string,
    description: string,
    heroImage: string,
    about: { heading: string, content: string[], images?: Array<{src,alt}> },
    carousel: { heading: string, maxHeight: string, items: CarouselItem[] },
  }
  ```
  `CarouselItem`: `{ src, displaySrc?, alt, caption?, description? }`.
- `data/people.js` uses `formatPersonAcademicInfo(person)` for display; keep shape
  `{ name, major, gradYear, email, image }`.
- `data/photos.js` is a nested plain object. Don't flatten it.

### Routing
- Adding a new static route = create `app/<name>/page.js` (default export React component).
- Adding a new team page = add an entry to `data/teamData.js` with a new `slug`. The dynamic
  route (`app/team/[slug]/page.js`) already has `generateStaticParams` consuming `teamData`.
- `trailingSlash: true` means routes emit as `foo/index.html`. Static hosts like DreamHost
  resolve `/foo/` cleanly.

### Client vs Server components
- Every component that uses hooks or browser APIs starts with `'use client';`. Most do.
- `app/layout.js` is a server component; it imports `AppShell` (client) to wrap children.
- Do not mark a server component `'use client'` unless you're certain.

### Accessibility
- Existing components use sensible `aria-label`s on icon buttons and `role`s on groups
  (see `TeamCarousel`). Preserve those when editing.

---

## 5. Common task patterns

### "Change the text on the homepage that says X"
1. Grep for X in `data/homeContent.js`.
2. If found, edit there — done.
3. If not found, grep in `components/` — it may be a hardcoded string; hoist it into
   `data/homeContent.js` as part of the fix.

### "Change an image"
1. Drop the new file into the appropriate `public/` subfolder.
2. Update the corresponding path in `data/photos.js`.
3. Rebuild; no component change needed unless you're adding a new image slot.

### "Add a new sub-team"
1. Add an entry to `data/teamData.js` with a unique `slug`, populated `about` and `carousel`.
2. Add photos under `public/images/...` and register them in `data/photos.js`.
3. Add leads under `teamLeaders[<slug>]` in `data/people.js`.
4. Add the new team card to `homeContent.teamsSection.teams` in `data/homeContent.js`.
5. `npm run build` — the dynamic route regenerates.

### "Change carousel caption position / size"
See `components/templates/TeamCarousel.js` and the `.carouselLayout*` classes in
`components/templates/Templates.module.css`. Orientation is derived from the **natural**
image dimensions loaded via `<img>`, not from config. If you want to force an orientation,
add a per-item override in `data/teamData.js` and plumb it through.

### "Optimize performance / reduce bundle size"
- Biggest wins: image compression (TinyPNG) since `images.unoptimized: true` means the
  browser downloads raw files.
- Check `npm run build` output for any route over ~200 KB First Load JS.
- Lazy-dynamic-import heavy libs (GSAP plugins are already deferred in `AppShell.js`).

### "Add an API / form submission / dynamic content"
You can't at runtime (static export). Options:
- Use an external form service (Formspree, Netlify Forms, Google Forms embed).
- Call a separate backend via `fetch` from a client component.
- Host a small backend elsewhere and point to it.

---

## 6. Recovery procedures

### `npm install` succeeds but something is missing from `node_modules`
```bash
rm -rf node_modules package-lock.json
/opt/homebrew/opt/node@22/bin/npm install
```
If you specifically need to keep `package-lock.json` stable, just delete `node_modules` alone.

### `Module not found: Can't resolve './...mjs'` in `vendor/framer-motion`
iCloud partially synced. Re-extract:
```bash
rm -rf vendor/framer-motion
tar -xzf framer-motion-11.18.2.tgz -C /tmp/
mv /tmp/package vendor/framer-motion
```

### `.next 2/`, `.next-dev 3/`, `.next-stale-*/` appearing
iCloud conflict copies. `rm -rf` any of them; they're cruft.

### `ERR_INVALID_PACKAGE_CONFIG` during build
You're on Node 24. Use Node 22:
```bash
PATH="/opt/homebrew/opt/node@22/bin:$PATH" npm run build
```

### Build succeeds but page looks stale
Browser or CDN cache. Hard refresh; if deploying to DreamHost, wait for their CDN TTL or
purge via their panel.

---

## 7. Testing & verification

**There are no automated tests in this repo.** Verification is manual:

1. `npm run dev`, visit affected routes at http://localhost:3000.
2. Hard-refresh after code changes if you disabled auto-reload.
3. `npm run build` to confirm static export succeeds. A successful build lists every route
   with its size — check for unexpected ∗Server∗ markers (everything should be ○ Static or
   ● SSG).
4. Optional: `npx http-server out/` (or `python3 -m http.server -d out 8080`) to spot-check
   the actual exported HTML.

If you introduce real logic and want tests, Vitest + Testing Library would fit; no framework
is installed yet — that's a deliberate tradeoff for a content-heavy marketing site.

---

## 8. Deployment (short form)

```bash
npm run build
rsync -avz --delete out/ USER@SERVER:/path/to/webroot/
```

Upload the **contents** of `out/`, not `out/` itself. `index.html` belongs at the web root.
DreamHost is the current host; Netlify / Vercel / Cloudflare Pages / S3+CloudFront all work
with the same artifact. See `README.md` §Deployment for specifics.

---

## 9. Things you should probably not do without asking

- Upgrade Next to 15.x.
- Swap CSS Modules for Tailwind / styled-components.
- Remove `vendor/framer-motion` or the `lib/framer-motion.js` shim.
- Delete `scripts/prepare-next-runtime.mjs` — it exists for a real iCloud reason.
- Move the repo off iCloud Desktop (breaks the owner's setup, not your call).
- Push directly to `main` without running `npm run build` first.
- Commit `out/`, `node_modules/`, `.next*/`, or any macOS ` N` duplicate file.

---

## 10. Current state snapshot (for grounding)

- Main branch: `main` on `github.com/cifyr/DBFApp`.
- Last verified build: Next 14.2.35 on Node v22.22.2, 14 static routes rendered, `out/` is
  ~23 MB.
- Notable uncommitted-at-time-of-last-audit files: multiple `.next N` / `.next-dev N`
  duplicates, `app/layout 2.js` stale duplicate, numerous " 2" duplicated images under
  `public/`. Treat ` N`-suffixed files as iCloud garbage unless you specifically confirm otherwise.
- Known warning at install: `@studio-freight/lenis@1.0.42` is deprecated — the package has
  been renamed to `lenis`. Not urgent but worth flagging in a dep update PR.

End of briefing. When in doubt, prefer reading `data/*.js` and the component that consumes
it before changing anything.
